# Build-context excludes for the telemetry stack.
#
# Both `ingest` and every processor image (field_enricher, gps_classifier,
# lap_timer, track_mapper, gg_plot) use this directory (telmtry/) as their
# Docker build context. Without this file the whole 3.4 GB tree — including the
# 1.1 GB Next.js node_modules and 546 MB of runtime logs — is tarred and shipped
# to the daemon on EVERY build, and churning files (logs, node_modules) bust the
# layer cache. None of the entries below are ever COPYed into these images:
#   * node_modules / .next  → frontend only; these are Python images
#   * logs                  → mounted as a runtime volume, not built in
#   * __pycache__ / *.pyc   → regenerated inside the image
#   * .git                  → never needed at build time
#
# If a future image legitimately needs something excluded here, whitelist it
# with a `!pattern` line at the bottom rather than deleting this file.

# --- frontend / JS build artifacts (the big one: ~1.1 GB) ---
**/node_modules
**/.next
**/.turbo
**/dist
**/.cache
**/coverage

# --- runtime logs (~546 MB) ---
logs/
**/*.log

# --- python caches ---
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/.pytest_cache
**/.mypy_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/.venv
**/venv

# --- vcs / editor / os cruft ---
.git
.gitignore
**/.DS_Store
**/.idea
**/.vscode

# --- this tooling itself doesn't need to be in the image ---
**/*.md
